      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BETTORBUST (3) settled in the leading division and finished well but could only manage second last start over 1690m at Shepparton, failing to emulate his success at this track the run before. Has the benefit of a good draw. Good enough to take out a race like this. OZZIE DAYBREAK (9) has raced two times this campaign and has filled a minor placing on each occasion. Registered yet another strong performance last start when he battled on bravely to just miss out over 1750m at Swan Hill, adding to a string of recent minor placings. Not drawn to best so may need a 10/10 drive. Big chance based on what we have seen of late. FLAME BLASTER (2) has to come into calculations on the back of some strong recent form, most recently when second at this track over 1790m. Must be included. SHES POPPY (11) is the best of the rest after finishing runner-up over 1790m at this track last time out.",
